<check_type:"Unix">

<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "Oracle Linux 8 platform check"
      file        : "/etc/system-release"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*Oracle[\\s]+Linux.*release"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*Oracle[\\s]+Linux.*release[\\s]+@PLATFORM_VERSION@"
    </custom_item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "CIS_Oracle_Linux_8_STIG_v1.0.0_CAT_II.audit from CIS Oracle Linux 8 STIG v1.0.0"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      show_output : YES
    </report>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description     : "auth"
          file            : "/etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d/*.conf"
          regex           : "^[^#]*auth\\.\\*"
          expect          : "^[^#]*auth\\.\\*"
          required        : NO
          min_occurrences : "1"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description     : "authpriv"
          file            : "/etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d/*.conf"
          regex           : "^[^#]*authpriv\\.\\*"
          expect          : "^[^#]*authpriv\\.\\*"
          required        : NO
          min_occurrences : "1"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type            : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description     : "daemon"
          file            : "/etc/rsyslog.conf /etc/rsyslog.d/*.conf"
          regex           : "^[^#]*daemon\\.\\*"
          expect          : "^[^#]*daemon\\.\\*"
          required        : NO
          min_occurrences : "1"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.10 OL08-00-010070"
          info        : "All OL 8 remote access methods must be monitored.

GROUP ID: V-248530
RULE ID: SV-248530r958406

Remote access services, such as those providing remote access to network devices and information systems, which lack automated monitoring capabilities increase risk and make remote user access management difficult at best.

Remote access is access to DOD nonpublic information systems by an authorized user (or an information system) communicating through an external, nonorganization-controlled network. Remote access methods include, for example, dial-up, broadband, and wireless.

Automated monitoring of remote access sessions allows organizations to detect cyberattacks and ensure ongoing compliance with remote access policies by auditing connection activities of remote access capabilities, such as Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP), on a variety of information system components (e.g., servers, workstations, notebook computers, smartphones, and tablets)."
          solution    : "Configure OL 8 to monitor all remote access methods by installing rsyslog with the following command:

$ sudo yum install rsyslog

Add or update the following lines to the \"/etc/rsyslog.conf\" file:

auth.*;authpriv.*;daemon.* /var/log/secure

The \"rsyslog\" service must be restarted for the changes to take effect. To restart the \"rsyslog\" service, run the following command:

$ sudo systemctl restart rsyslog.service"
          reference   : "800-171|3.1.12,800-171r3|03.01.12,800-53|AC-17(1),800-53r5|AC-17(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000067,CN-L3|8.1.4.4(c),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(i),CSF|PR.AC-3,CSF|PR.PT-4,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.16,ISO/IEC-27001|A.6.2.2,ITSG-33|AC-17(1),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.4.4,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,Rule-ID|SV-248530r958406_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010070,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.6,Vuln-ID|V-248530"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>
    </if>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.100 OL08-00-010570"
      info        : "OL 8 must prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed on file systems that contain user home directories.

GROUP ID: V-248616
RULE ID: SV-248616r991589

The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system not to execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
      solution    : "Configure \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nosuid\" option on file systems that contain user home directories for interactive users."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248616r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010570,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248616"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+@HOME_MOUNT@[\\s]"
      expect      : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+@HOME_MOUNT@[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]*nosuid"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CHECK_NOT
          description : "Check that /sys/firmware/efi does not exist"
          file        : "/sys/firmware/efi"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "1.101 OL08-00-010571"
          info        : "OL 8 must prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed on the /boot directory.

GROUP ID: V-248617
RULE ID: SV-248617r991589

The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system not to execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
          solution    : "Configure the \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nosuid\" option on the /boot directory."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248617r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010571,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248617"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
          file        : "/etc/fstab"
          regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot[\\s]"
          expect      : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]*nosuid"
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.101 OL08-00-010571"
          info        : "OL 8 must prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed on the /boot directory.

GROUP ID: V-248617
RULE ID: SV-248617r991589

The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system not to execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
          solution    : "Configure the \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nosuid\" option on the /boot directory."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248617r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010571,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248617"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
        </report>
      </else>
    </if>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CHECK
          description : "Check if BIOS/UEFI"
          file        : "/sys/firmware/efi"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "1.102 OL08-00-010572"
          info        : "OL 8 must prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed on the /boot/efi directory.

GROUP ID: V-248618
RULE ID: SV-248618r991589

The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system not to execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
          solution    : "Configure the \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nosuid\" option on the /boot/efi directory."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248618r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010572,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248618"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
          file        : "/etc/fstab"
          regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot/efi[\\s]"
          expect      : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot/efi[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]*nosuid"
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.102 OL08-00-010572"
          info        : "OL 8 must prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed on the /boot/efi directory.

GROUP ID: V-248618
RULE ID: SV-248618r991589

The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system not to execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
          solution    : "Configure the \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nosuid\" option on the /boot/efi directory."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248618r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010572,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248618"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
        </report>
      </else>
    </if>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.103 OL08-00-010580"
      info        : "OL 8 must prevent special devices on non-root local partitions.

GROUP ID: V-248619RULE ID: SV-248619r991589

The \"nodev\" mount option causes the system to not interpret character or block special devices. Executing character or block special devices from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access. The only legitimate location for device files is the /dev directory located on the root partition."
      solution    : "Configure the \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nodev\" option on all non-root local partitions."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248619r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010580,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248619"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      cmd         : "/bin/mount | /bin/grep -P '^/dev[\\S]* on /[\\S]+' | /bin/grep --invert-match 'nodev' | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"nodev has been set appropriately for mounted /dev file systems\"; else print \"fail - nodev option not found on the following file systems\"}'"
      expect      : "^nodev has been set appropriately for mounted /dev file systems$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.104 OL08-00-010590"
      info        : "OL 8 file systems that contain user home directories must not execute binary files.

GROUP ID: V-248620
RULE ID: SV-248620r991589

The \"noexec\" mount option causes the system not to execute binary files. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved binary files, as they may be incompatible. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for unprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
