      perm        : "-0002"
    </custom_item>

    <item>
      description : "1.122 OL08-00-010720"
      info        : "All OL 8 local interactive users must have a home directory assigned in the \"/etc/passwd\" file.

GROUP ID: V-248638
RULE ID: SV-248638r991589

If local interactive users are not assigned a valid home directory, there is no place for the storage and control of files they should own."
      solution    : "Assign home directories to all local interactive users on OL 8 that currently do not have a home directory assigned."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248638r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010720,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248638"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      name        : "active_accounts_without_home_dir"
    </item>

    <item>
      description : "1.123 OL08-00-010730"
      info        : "All OL 8 local interactive user home directories must have mode \"0750\" or less permissive.

GROUP ID: V-248639
RULE ID: SV-248639r991589

Excessive permissions on local interactive user home directories may allow unauthorized access to user files by other users."
      solution    : "Change the mode of interactive users' home directories to \"0750\" using the following command.

Note: The example will be for the user \"smithj\".

$ sudo chmod 0750 /home/smithj"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248639r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010730,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248639"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      name        : "accounts_bad_home_permissions"
      mask        : "7027"
      ignore_user : "nobody"
      uid_ge      : "1000"
    </item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FIND_CMD
      description : "1.124 OL08-00-010731"
      info        : "All OL 8 local interactive user home directory files must have mode \"0750\" or less permissive.

GROUP ID: V-248640
RULE ID: SV-248640r991589

Excessive permissions on local interactive user home directories may allow unauthorized access to user files by other users."
      solution    : "Set the mode on files and directories in the local interactive user home directory with the following command:

Note: The example will be for the user smithj, who has a home directory of \"/home/smithj\" and is a member of the users group.

$ sudo chmod 0750 /home/smithj/<file or directory>"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248640r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010731,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248640"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      not_expect  : "^.*\\s+7[567][1-7]\\s*$"
      exec        : "/bin/stat -c \"%n %a\" '{}' \\;"
      find_type   : "f"
      perm        : "-0750"
      target      : "~"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.125 OL08-00-010740"
      info        : "All OL 8 local interactive user home directories must be group-owned by the home directory owner's primary group.

GROUP ID: V-248641RULE ID: SV-248641r991589

If the Group Identifier (GID) of a local interactive user's home directory is not the same as the primary GID of the user, this would allow unauthorized access to the user's files. Users that share the same group may not be able to access files to which they legitimately should have access."
      solution    : "Change the group owner of a local interactive user's home directory to the group found in \"/etc/passwd\" using the following command.

Note: The example will be for the user \"smithj\", who has a home directory of \"/home/smithj\" and has a primary group of users.

$ sudo chgrp users /home/smithj"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248641r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010740,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248641"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      cmd         : "home_dirs=`/bin/awk -F: '($3>=1000)&&($7 !~ /nologin/)&&($1 !~ /nobody/){print $6}' /etc/passwd | /bin/sort -u`; for dirs in $home_dirs; do g=$(/bin/stat -c %G $dirs); o=$(/bin/stat -c %U $dirs); p=$(/bin/id -gn $o); if [ $p != $g ]; then echo \"${dirs} group-owned by ${g} (should be owned by ${p})\"; fi; done | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR <= 0) print \"All local interactive user home directories have correct group ownership\"}'"
      expect      : "^All local interactive user home directories have correct group ownership$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.126 OL08-00-010760"
      info        : "All OL 8 local interactive user accounts must be assigned a home directory upon creation.

GROUP ID: V-248644
RULE ID: SV-248644r991589

If local interactive users are not assigned a valid home directory, there is no place for the storage and control of files they should own."
      solution    : "Configure OL 8 to assign home directories to all new local interactive users by setting the \"CREATE_HOME\" parameter in \"/etc/login.defs\" to \"yes\" as follows.

CREATE_HOME yes"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248644r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010760,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248644"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      file        : "/etc/login.defs"
      regex       : "(?i)^[\\s]*CREATE_HOME[\\s]*"
      expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*CREATE_HOME[\\s]*@CREATE_HOME@[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <item>
      description : "1.127 OL08-00-010750"
      info        : "All OL 8 local interactive user home directories defined in the \"/etc/passwd\" file must exist.

GROUP ID: V-248643
RULE ID: SV-248643r991589

If a local interactive user has a home directory defined that does not exist, the user may be given access to the \"/\" directory as the current working directory upon logon. This could create a denial of service because the user would not be able to access their logon configuration files, and it may give them visibility to system files they normally would not be able to access."
      solution    : "Create home directories to all local interactive users that currently do not have a home directory assigned. Use the following commands to create the user home directory assigned in \"/etc/ passwd\".

Note: The example will be for the user smithj, who has a home directory of \"/home/smithj\", a UID of \"smithj\", and a Group Identifier (GID) of \"users assigned\" in \"/etc/passwd\".

$ sudo mkdir /home/smithj $ sudo chown smithj /home/smithj $ sudo chgrp users /home/smithj $ sudo chmod 0750 /home/smithj"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248643r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010750,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248643"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      name        : "active_accounts_without_home_dir"
    </item>

    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "1.128 OL08-00-010741"
      info        : "OL 8 must be configured so that all files and directories contained in local interactive user home directories are group-owned by a group of which the home directory owner is a member.

GROUP ID: V-248642
RULE ID: SV-248642r991589

If a local interactive user's files are group-owned by a group of which the user is not a member, unintended users may be able to access them.

NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "Change the group of a local interactive user's files and directories to a group that the interactive user is a member. To change the group owner of a local interactive user's files and directories, use the following command:

Note: The example will be for the user smithj, who has a home directory of \"/home/smithj\" and is a member of the users group.

$ sudo chgrp smithj /home/smithj/<file or directory>"
