    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.14 OL08-00-010120"
      info        : "OL 8 must employ FIPS 140-2 approved cryptographic hashing algorithms for all stored passwords.

GROUP ID: V-248534
RULE ID: SV-248534r1015029

The system must use a strong hashing algorithm to store the password.

Passwords need to be protected at all times, and encryption is the standard method for protecting passwords. If passwords are not encrypted, they can be plainly read (i.e., clear text) and easily compromised."
      solution    : "Lock all interactive user accounts not using SHA-512 hashing until the passwords can be regenerated with SHA-512."
      reference   : "800-171|3.5.2,800-171r3|03.05.07,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000196,CCI|CCI-004062,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.17,ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-248534r1015029_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-010120,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1,Vuln-ID|V-248534"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      cmd         : "/bin/cut -d: -f1,2 /etc/shadow | /bin/grep -Pv ':[*!\\$]' | /bin/grep -Pv '^\\$6\\$' | /bin/awk -F: '{print $1} END {if (NR == 0) print \"All interactive user passwords are encrypted\"; else print \"There are interactive user passwords that are not encrypted\"}'"
      expect      : "^All interactive user passwords are encrypted$"
    </custom_item>

