    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.178 OL08-00-020180"
      info        : "OL 8 passwords for new users or password changes must have a 24 hours/one day minimum password lifetime restriction in \"/etc/shadow\".

GROUP ID: V-248694RULE ID: SV-248694r1015054

Enforcing a minimum password lifetime helps to prevent repeated password changes to defeat the password reuse or history enforcement requirement. If users are allowed to immediately and continually change their password, the password could be repeatedly changed in a short period of time to defeat the organization's policy regarding password reuse."
      solution    : "Configure non-compliant accounts to enforce a 24 hours/one day minimum password lifetime:

$ sudo chage -m 1 [user]"
      reference   : "800-171|3.5.2,800-171r3|03.05.07,800-53|IA-5(1),800-53r5|IA-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000198,CCI|CCI-004066,CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.17,ITSG-33|IA-5(1),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T5.2.3,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-248694r1015054_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-020180,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.1,Vuln-ID|V-248694"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      cmd         : "v1=$(/bin/awk '/^UID_MIN/ {print $2}' /etc/login.defs);/bin/awk -v \"uidmin=${v1}\" -F: 'FILENAME == \"/etc/passwd\" { if ($3 >= uidmin && $3 < 65534) users[$1] } FILENAME == \"/etc/shadow\" { if ($1 in users && $4 < 1) badusers[$1]; } END { if (length(badusers) > 0){ for (user in badusers) {print user} } else { print \"No users found\" } }' /etc/passwd /etc/shadow"
      expect      : "^No users found$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.179 OL08-00-020190"
      info        : "OL 8 passwords for new users or password changes must have a 24 hours/one day minimum password lifetime restriction in \"/etc/login.defs\".

GROUP ID: V-248695
RULE ID: SV-248695r1015055

Enforcing a minimum password lifetime helps to prevent repeated password changes to defeat the password reuse or history enforcement requirement. If users are allowed to immediately and continually change their password, the password could be repeatedly changed in a short period of time to defeat the organization's policy regarding password reuse."
      solution    : "Configure OL 8 to enforce 24 hours/one day as the minimum password lifetime.

Add the following line in \"/etc/login.defs\" (or modify the line to have the required value):

PASS_MIN_DAYS 1"
