    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.214 OL08-00-030070"
      info        : "OL 8 audit logs must have a mode of \"0600\" or less permissive to prevent unauthorized read access.

GROUP ID: V-248732
RULE ID: SV-248732r958434

Unauthorized disclosure of audit records can reveal system and configuration data to attackers, thus compromising its confidentiality.

Audit information includes all information (e.g., audit records, audit settings, audit reports) needed to successfully audit OL 8 activity.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028, SRG-OS-000059-GPOS-00029"
      solution    : "Configure the audit log to be protected from unauthorized read access by setting the correct permissive mode with the following command:

$ sudo chmod 0600 [audit_log_file]

Replace \"[audit_log_file]\" to the correct audit log path. By default, this location is \"/var/log/audit/audit.log\"."
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.8,800-171r3|03.03.08,800-53|AU-9,800-53r5|AU-9a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000162,CCI|CCI-000163,CCI|CCI-000164,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(d),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(f),CN-L3|8.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(c),CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.4.2,ITSG-33|AU-9,LEVEL|2M,NESA|M5.2.3,NESA|M5.5.2,NESA|T3.6.4,NESA|T8.2.9,NIAv2|SM5,NIAv2|SM6,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.5,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.5.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.3.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-248732r958434_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-030070,Vuln-ID|V-248732"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      cmd         : "logfile=$(/bin/grep -iw ^\\s*log_file /etc/audit/auditd.conf); if [ ! -z \"${logfile}\" ]; then /bin/stat -c \"%n %a\" $(/bin/dirname ${logfile} | /bin/grep \"/\")/* | /bin/grep -Ev '[^1-7][0-6]00' | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"All files have a mode of 0600 or less\"; else print \"Failing files found\"}'; else echo \"log_file variable in /etc/audit/auditd.conf not set\"; fi"
      expect      : "^All files have a mode of 0600 or less$"
    </custom_item>

