    <custom_item>
      type        : RPM_CHECK
      description : "1.322 OL08-00-040135"
      info        : "The OL 8 \"fapolicy\" module must be installed.

GROUP ID: V-248859
RULE ID: SV-248859r958804

The organization must identify authorized software programs and permit execution of authorized software. The process used to identify software programs that are authorized to execute on organizational information systems is commonly referred to as whitelisting.

Using a whitelist provides a configuration management method for allowing the execution of only authorized software. Using only authorized software decreases risk by limiting the number of potential vulnerabilities. Verification of whitelisted software occurs prior to execution or at system startup.

Users' home directories/folders may contain information of a sensitive nature. Non-privileged users should coordinate any sharing of information with a System Administrator through shared resources.

OL 8 ships with many optional packages. One such package is a file access policy daemon called \"fapolicyd\". This is a userspace daemon that determines access rights to files based on attributes of the process and file. It can be used to either blacklist or whitelist processes or file access.

Proceed with caution with enforcing the use of this daemon. Improper configuration may render the system non-functional. The \"fapolicyd\" API is not namespace aware and can cause issues when launching or running containers.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154, SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155"
      solution    : "Install \"fapolicyd\" with the following command:

$ sudo yum install fapolicyd.x86_64"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.7,800-171|3.4.8,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.08,800-53|CM-7(2),800-53|CM-7(5),800-53r5|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(5),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CCI|CCI-001774,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.5.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.6.2,ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7(2),LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-248859r958804_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-040135,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,TBA-FIISB|44.2.2,TBA-FIISB|49.2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248859"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      rpm         : "fapolicyd-0.0.0-0"
      operator    : "gt"
      required    : YES
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.323 OL08-00-040136"
      info        : "The OL 8 \"fapolicy\" module must be enabled.

GROUP ID: V-248860
RULE ID: SV-248860r958804

The organization must identify authorized software programs and permit execution of authorized software. The process used to identify software programs that are authorized to execute on organizational information systems is commonly referred to as whitelisting.

Using a whitelist provides a configuration management method for allowing the execution of only authorized software. Using only authorized software decreases risk by limiting the number of potential vulnerabilities. Verification of whitelisted software occurs prior to execution or at system startup.

Users' home directories/folders may contain information of a sensitive nature. Non-privileged users should coordinate any sharing of information with a System Administrator through shared resources.

OL 8 ships with many optional packages. One such package is a file access policy daemon called \"fapolicyd\". This is a userspace daemon that determines access rights to files based on attributes of the process and file. It can be used to either blacklist or whitelist processes or file access.

Proceed with caution with enforcing the use of this daemon. Improper configuration may render the system non-functional. The \"fapolicyd\" API is not namespace aware and can cause issues when launching or running containers.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154, SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155"
      solution    : "Enable \"fapolicyd\" using the following command:

$ sudo systemctl enable --now fapolicyd"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.7,800-171|3.4.8,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.08,800-53|CM-7(2),800-53|CM-7(5),800-53r5|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(5),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CCI|CCI-001774,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.5.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.6.2,ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7(2),LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-248860r958804_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-040136,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,TBA-FIISB|44.2.2,TBA-FIISB|49.2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248860"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      cmd         : "/bin/systemctl status fapolicyd.service"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*Active:[\\s]*active[\\s]*\\(running\\)"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "permissive"
          file        : "/etc/fapolicyd/fapolicyd.conf"
          regex       : "^[\\s]*permissive[\\s]*="
          expect      : "^[\\s]*permissive[\\s]*=[\\s]*0[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "deny all all"
          cmd         : "/bin/tail -1 /etc/fapolicyd/fapolicyd.rules 2>/dev/null;/bin/tail -1 /etc/fapolicyd/compiled.rules 2>/dev/null"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*deny[\\s]+perm[\\s]*=[\\s]*any[\\s]+all[\\s]*:[\\s]*all[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.324 OL08-00-040137"
          info        : "The OL 8 fapolicy module must be configured to employ a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs.

GROUP ID: V-248861
RULE ID: SV-248861r958804

The organization must identify authorized software programs and permit execution of authorized software. The process used to identify software programs that are authorized to execute on organizational information systems is commonly referred to as whitelisting.

Using a whitelist provides a configuration management method for allowing the execution of only authorized software. Using only authorized software decreases risk by limiting the number of potential vulnerabilities. Verification of whitelisted software occurs prior to execution or at system startup.

Users' home directories/folders may contain information of a sensitive nature. Non-privileged users should coordinate any sharing of information with a System Administrator through shared resources.

OL 8 ships with many optional packages. One such package is a file access policy daemon called \"fapolicyd\". This is a userspace daemon that determines access rights to files based on attributes of the process and file. It can be used to either blacklist or whitelist processes or file access.

Proceed with caution with enforcing the use of this daemon. Improper configuration may render the system non-functional. The \"fapolicyd\" API is not namespace aware and can cause issues when launching or running containers.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154, SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155"
          solution    : "Configure OL 8 to employ a deny-all, permit-by-exception application whitelisting policy with \"fapolicyd\".

With the \"fapolicyd\" installed and enabled, configure the daemon to function in permissive mode until the whitelist is built correctly to avoid system lockout. Do this by editing the \"/etc/fapolicyd/fapolicyd.conf\" file with the following line:

permissive = 1

For OL 8.4 systems and older:Build the whitelist in the \"/etc/fapolicyd/fapolicyd.rules\" file ensuring the last rule is

deny perm=any all : all

For OL 8.5 systems and newer:Build the whitelist in a file within the \"/etc/fapolicyd/rules.d\" directory ensuring the last rule is

deny perm=any all : all

Once it is determined the whitelist is built correctly, set the fapolicyd to enforcing mode by editing the \"permissive\" line in the /etc/fapolicyd/fapolicyd.conf file.

permissive = 0"
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.7,800-171|3.4.8,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.08,800-53|CM-7(2),800-53|CM-7(5),800-53r5|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(5),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CCI|CCI-001774,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.5.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.6.2,ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7(2),LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-248861r958804_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-040137,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,TBA-FIISB|44.2.2,TBA-FIISB|49.2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248861"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>
    </if>

